      "design": "r1A",
      "good": "The equal metric columns make EN, ZH, and AR easy to compare. The shared header fits in three lines, and the notes remain readable without breaking words. Rows have a reasonably compact rhythm.",
      "problems": "The Small row is much taller than the Base row, while the Notes column takes nearly half the table. That allocation is justified by the prose, though it leaves relatively generous space around the short accuracy values.",
      "cause": "The 205px Notes column wraps the Small note to three lines; the three 60px metric columns give the shared header enough combined width to stay at three lines."
    },
    {
      "design": "r1B",
      "good": "The equal metric columns give the language measures a clear, consistent rhythm, and the shared header fits in three lines.",
      "problems": "The Small note becomes a four-line block, creating a conspicuously tall row and weakening the table's vertical rhythm. The extra metric width does little for the short values.",
      "cause": "Increasing each metric column to 65px leaves only 190px for Notes, forcing an extra line in the Small note."
    },
    {
      "design": "r1C",
      "good": "The wider Notes column gives the prose more breathing room, and the equal metric widths preserve the comparison structure.",
      "problems": "The shared header wraps to four lines, making the header block disproportionately tall. The wider Notes column does not reduce the visible Small or Large notes below three and two lines respectively.",
      "cause": "The three 57px metric columns provide too little combined width for the shared header to retain its three-line wrap."
    }
  ],
  "done": false,
